-- title:
--   Properness of the two-chart integral model over A₁
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a non-unit. The hypotheses come in groups, summarised here: a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ consisting exactly of the supersingular places $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\ q\ M'$; the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of the base-changed level-$M'$ modular function field along $A$, together with its compatibility with coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series; a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ and families $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$, with their explicit description at $\mathrm{lineInfty}$, transitivity and injectivity properties, $\Gamma_0(M')$-equivariance under the automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$, contraction to $A$, reduction compatibility with $R_0$ and with places in $W$, and a translation-unit element; a regular prolongation $R$ with $R.\mathrm{integers}=O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ and $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ the preimage of that ring; an element $\pi$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ in $A$; a subfield $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ such that $A\cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field and $k_0\cap A\to A/\mathfrak m_A$ is onto; an auxiliary prime $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$, a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity $\zeta_0\in k_0$ and $\varpi_t\in k_0\cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\cdot(\text{unit})$. Finally let $K_1$ be a finite extension of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ the valuation subring of $K_1$ cut out by $A$, assumed a henselian discrete valuation ring. Give $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ the $k_0$-algebra structure through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ that together with the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generates everything, is stable under all $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, is linearly disjoint from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over every finite $k_0$-subextension $K'$ in the stated sense, and contains every element of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with rational $q$-expansion: for any $A_1$-algebra structure on the compositum $K_1\cdot F_0$ compatible with the inclusion $K_1\hookrightarrow\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and any nonzero $j_1$ in $K_1\cdot F_0$ equal to the image of the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$ of the modular invariant, the structure morphism $\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase}$ from the pushout of $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the two chart algebras generated over $A_1$ by $j_1$ and by $j_1^{-1}$ to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$ is proper.
--
--   This is the properness input for the integral model of the level-$(q^2M',H)$ modular curve over the discrete valuation ring $A_1=A\cap K_1$, obtained from the general properness criterion for two-chart integral models once both chart algebras are of finite type, which follows from transcendence of $j_1$ over $k_0$ and finiteness of $K_1\cdot F_0$ over $k_0(j_1)$. It discharges the properness hypothesis in the centring and branch-reading steps of the Igusa-component covering argument.
